From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mosip-vivid <vivid@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:28:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] liveness: operator login adds face liveness and
 enrolled-face matching

- LoginPage._getLoginAction: after the password is accepted, run an
  OPERATOR liveness session and match the live face (anchor embedding)
  against the operator's onboarded face. On failure the session is
  logged out and the reason is shown.
- ArcEnrolledFaceProvider: reads user_biometric FACE rows for the user,
  decodes the stored ISO 19794-5 record (IsoFaceImages); the bridge
  embeds it with the same MobileFaceNet and compares cosine similarity
  with mosip.registration.liveness.operator.faceMatch.threshold
  (default 0.50). faceMatch.requireEnrolment (default false) decides
  whether an operator without an enrolled face may log in on liveness
  alone; both outcomes are audited (LIVENESS_FACE_MATCH_*).
